From 68563f7c8be603264550174de09577722a6cc6bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:58:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/89] sovereignos: fix UserBackupManagerService using wrong
 Context for CE-storage check

UserBackupPreferences's constructor calls Context#getSharedPreferences(),
which checks whether *that context's own implicit user* has unlocked CE
storage. Line 622 passed mContext (BackupManagerService's construction-time
context, implicitly user 0) instead of userContext (created two lines
above, specifically scoped to mUserId, for exactly this kind of per-user
check) -- a plain wrong-variable bug, present in upstream AOSP since 2019
(commit 9e111f19df8e5, confirmed via git blame; never touched by any
sovereignos patch, confirmed via git log --grep=^sovereignos on this path).

Harmless on every ordinary Android flow, because user 0 is always already
unlocked by the time any other user's backup service starts -- you must
unlock the primary user to even reach the multi-user switcher UI. SovereignOS's
Duress Unlock decoy-routing mechanism is the first and only path that
starts a secondary user's (the decoy's) backup service while user 0 has
never been credential-unlocked this boot, which throws
IllegalStateException from ContextImpl.credentialProtectedStorageCheck()
in the backup HandlerThread, crashing system_server fatally and triggering
a full device reboot -- confirmed via real hardware reproduction: the
device's own event log shows uc_finish_user_unlocking/ssm_user_unlocking
firing for user 10 (the decoy), never 0, immediately before the crash,
ruling out any SovereignOS-authored code (DecoyProfileHelper, RealUserQuiescer
-- neither calls anything backup- or unlock-lifecycle-related) as the
trigger.

Fix: use userContext, matching the comment already on the line above it
("We need a context for the user in question") and the same pattern
already used for mConstants a few lines earlier in this same constructor.
---
 .../android/server/backup/UserBackupManagerService.java  | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/backup/java/com/android/server/backup/UserBackupManagerService.java b/services/backup/java/com/android/server/backup/UserBackupManagerService.java
index 18534563598b..ea020ca3df6d 100644
--- a/services/backup/java/com/android/server/backup/UserBackupManagerService.java
+++ b/services/backup/java/com/android/server/backup/UserBackupManagerService.java
@@ -619,7 +619,14 @@ public class UserBackupManagerService {
                 backupManagerMonitorDumpsysUtils::deleteExpiredBMMEvents,
                 INITIALIZATION_DELAY_MILLIS);
 
-        mBackupPreferences = new UserBackupPreferences(mContext, mBaseStateDir);
+        // Use userContext (created above), not mContext: mContext.getSharedPreferences()
+        // checks CE-storage-unlocked state for mContext's own implicit user, which is only
+        // ever correct here because on every ordinary Android flow user 0 is already unlocked
+        // by the time any other user's backup service starts. SovereignOS's Duress Unlock decoy
+        // switch is the first path that starts a secondary user's backup service while user 0
+        // has never unlocked this boot, which throws IllegalStateException from
+        // ContextImpl.credentialProtectedStorageCheck() and crashes system_server fatally.
+        mBackupPreferences = new UserBackupPreferences(userContext, mBaseStateDir);
 
         // Power management
         mWakelock =
